# Kickstart Fallback Implementation Plan

This plan introduces a new, high-confidence fallback layer in the `product.search` tool. When the AI is unsure about a category (Semantic Kickstart) and the filtered search fails, it will attempt one more "global" precision/vector search before giving up and showing relaxed suggestions.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change affects the search logic hierarchy. The "Kickstart Fallback" is treated as a **Real Match** (returning actual products) rather than a **Suggestion**, which means the bot will present these results as definitive matches.

## Proposed Changes

### Intent Pipeline

#### [MODIFY] [parameterExtractor.js](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/eCommerce/be3_ai/src/services/intentResolver/pipeline/parameterExtractor.js)
- Detect `source === 'SEMANTIC_KICKSTART'` during category extraction in `extractParameters`.
- Set `is_kickstart: true` in the returned parameters.

### Product Tool

#### [MODIFY] [product.js](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/eCommerce/be3_ai/src/tools/product.js)
- Add `is_kickstart` to the `product.search` parameter schema.
- Update the `handler` to implement the new fallback layer:
    1. **Stage 1 & Fallback 1** run as normal (category-filtered).
    2. **Kickstart Fallback (New)**: If results are zero, `is_kickstart` is true, and a query exists:
        - Log `TOOL:PRODUCT_KICKSTART_FALLBACK`.
        - Try Stage 1 again without `catId`.
        - If still zero, try Fallback 1 (Vector) again without `catId`.
        - If results found, return them immediately via `handleSearchResults`.
    3. **Fallback 2 (Suggestions)**: If no results yet, run the existing "Relaxed Search" (Attempt 1 & 2) which *keeps* the category.

